<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">East African campaign (World War II)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940–1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The East African campaign was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> campaign fought in 1940–1941 between British and Commonwealth forces, with Ethiopian resistance fighters, and the Italian forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a>. Its outcome destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-east-africa">Italian East Africa</a>, restored Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> to his throne and marked the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div>
